WEBVTT

00:01.620 --> 00:04.300
[GUNSHOTS]

00:04.340 --> 00:07.180
Elizabeth! Hey! What's going on?

00:12.840 --> 00:18.560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:18.560 --> 00:23.980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:30.540 --> 00:33.860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:33.860 --> 00:36.540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:36.540 --> 00:42.840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

00:42.840 --> 00:48.960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

00:48.960 --> 00:55.040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:55.180 --> 01:01.200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

01:01.340 --> 01:08.080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

01:08.260 --> 01:13.620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

01:13.840 --> 01:20.340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

01:20.340 --> 01:26.100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

01:26.100 --> 01:32.300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

01:32.300 --> 01:39.120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

01:39.120 --> 01:41.940
Subtitles from Mohamed610 corrected by somanypetals.

01:43.140 --> 01:45.500
So this piece of info was
supposed to be confidential...

01:45.500 --> 01:47.160
...but, whatever.

01:47.420 --> 01:51.380
Barry told me the Colonel's got a plan
to smoke out some military guys he's been after.

01:51.440 --> 01:53.680
The ones from "The Fifth" something or other.

01:54.600 --> 01:56.200
The Fifth Laboratory.

01:58.300 --> 01:59.240
Al?

01:59.820 --> 02:01.240
I gotta find him.

02:01.280 --> 02:04.040
This could lead us straight to the
person who killed Lieutenant Hughes.

02:04.400 --> 02:05.260
Huh?!

02:05.280 --> 02:08.340
Hey, not so fast!
Tell me your secret first!

02:09.000 --> 02:10.740
I'll tell you when I get back, okay?

02:11.000 --> 02:13.600
Oh, come on! That's so unfair!

02:14.800 --> 02:16.080
I'll be back soon.

02:18.560 --> 02:21.060
Okay. Just be careful.

02:21.860 --> 02:24.300
I will. I promise.

02:30.840 --> 02:33.020
[GUN CLICKING EMPTY]

02:35.280 --> 02:37.360
Are you all done now?

02:38.000 --> 02:40.680
Then it's time to eat you.

02:43.900 --> 02:45.260
[BARKING]

02:45.260 --> 02:47.060
[GROWLING]

02:51.360 --> 02:53.540
Stop it! That tickles!

02:53.960 --> 02:54.840
Catch!

02:57.660 --> 03:00.380
[GUNSHOTS]

03:03.740 --> 03:05.880
[GUN CLICKING EMPTY]

03:09.920 --> 03:15.080
Bullets gone? Goodie, goodie!
I get to have dinner and dessert!

03:24.500 --> 03:26.500
I barely made it.

03:26.860 --> 03:27.980
[RELIEVED EXHALE]

03:28.360 --> 03:29.600
Colonel!

03:29.660 --> 03:31.580
Why the hell did you leave your post?!

03:31.580 --> 03:32.240
Uh—!

03:32.820 --> 03:36.120
No matter what happened to us, you could
still have kept your involvement a secret!

03:36.160 --> 03:37.680
That was the whole idea, right?

03:37.780 --> 03:40.340
But you just come waltzing in here, plain as day!

03:40.340 --> 03:41.960
Are you a complete idiot?!

03:42.060 --> 03:46.420
MUSTANG: Yeah, fine, fine, that's it. I'm an idiot, happy?
[FUERY CHUCKLING]

03:48.300 --> 03:50.560
Who the heck was that fat guy?

03:51.260 --> 03:54.460
Colonel! The target's on the move, sir!

03:54.620 --> 03:57.520
Strike the camp, sergeant!
Don't leave a single trace!

03:57.760 --> 04:00.640
And you stay right by the
sergeant's side, Hayate Sir!

04:00.640 --> 04:01.800
- Sir!
- [BARKS]

04:02.060 --> 04:03.720
[FOOTSTEPS]

04:04.520 --> 04:05.220
Colonel.

04:05.400 --> 04:06.240
What is it?

04:06.820 --> 04:08.420
Thanks for saving us back there.

04:08.780 --> 04:12.000
Tell me later.
Let's just stay focused on the mission for now.

04:12.400 --> 04:13.000
Sir.

04:18.800 --> 04:19.700
Quick, get in!

04:19.780 --> 04:20.580
Yes, sir.

04:25.140 --> 04:27.560
Are you trying to go after
Mr. Hughes' murderer?

04:31.160 --> 04:32.100
You in?

04:32.540 --> 04:33.460
Yeah!

04:39.260 --> 04:40.400
Don't let him get away.

04:40.440 --> 04:41.960
He ain't going nowhere.

04:42.240 --> 04:43.200
[LAUGHS]

04:43.240 --> 04:45.160
My soul won't be able to rest.

04:45.240 --> 04:48.260
Not until I eviscerate that meatbag!

04:48.780 --> 04:52.640
So do you think we can expect another
appearance from that blubberbeast back there?

04:52.740 --> 04:55.480
I doubt it. I scorched him off the ledge.

04:56.000 --> 04:59.280
Yeah, and I shot him in the head,
but he didn't really seem to mind.

04:59.280 --> 05:00.000
[GASPS]

05:00.340 --> 05:03.100
He didn't have an Ouroboros tattoo, did he?

05:03.480 --> 05:04.940
A tattoo? Well...

05:05.000 --> 05:08.240
Actually, yeah. On his tongue.

05:09.900 --> 05:14.000
In that case, you were probably dealing with a Homunculus.

05:15.500 --> 05:17.160
[BARRY SCREAMING]

05:17.160 --> 05:18.360
Watch it, Mustang!

05:18.400 --> 05:21.340
Hold on a damn second.
What are you saying, Al?

05:21.500 --> 05:23.040
That's just not possible.

05:23.260 --> 05:27.180
Yeah, that's what I thought.
Until I got kidnapped by a Homunculus.

05:27.280 --> 05:28.980
He called himself Greed.

05:29.140 --> 05:32.360
One thing he told me
is that nothing is impossible.

05:33.220 --> 05:36.320
I know for a fact that they
have amazing healing powers.

05:36.500 --> 05:42.620
I watched Greed get the top half of his head knocked off,
but he was perfectly fine a minute later.

05:42.700 --> 05:44.080
They're real, all right.

05:44.380 --> 05:46.700
But I understand if you don't believe me.

05:46.800 --> 05:50.120
After what I just saw, I have to believe you.

05:50.180 --> 05:54.000
Hold on, I rendered Fatboy down
to a bubbling puddle back there.

05:54.060 --> 05:55.940
Are you telling me he's still alive?

05:56.520 --> 05:57.480
AL: Probably.

05:57.760 --> 05:59.440
MUSTANG: Tch. Wonderful!

05:59.440 --> 06:02.600
Just a never-ending
parade of freaks lately, huh?

06:15.160 --> 06:18.940
BARRY: My body ran in there.
Seems to think it can hide from me.

06:19.020 --> 06:20.780
MUSTANG: The Third Laboratory, huh?

06:21.660 --> 06:24.320
So this ties them directly to the military.

06:24.960 --> 06:27.960
That's all we need for now.
We're pulling back.

06:28.160 --> 06:30.540
BARRY: Well, you have fun with that!
MUSTANG: Get back here!

06:32.380 --> 06:34.320
HAVOC: That psycho stormed the building.

06:34.360 --> 06:36.580
Yep, it's our lucky day.

06:36.580 --> 06:37.400
Huh?

06:37.520 --> 06:38.820
[BARRY GIGGLING MANIACALLY]

06:38.820 --> 06:40.120
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

06:41.520 --> 06:42.940
Out of my way!

06:42.980 --> 06:46.020
I don't want any of your boring old skin and bones.

06:46.100 --> 06:48.880
I got me a special reunion to get to.

06:51.660 --> 06:54.280
All personnel must evacuate immediately!

06:55.060 --> 06:56.160
Um, Colonel?

06:56.380 --> 06:59.420
Stay back. The man who broke in is a deranged murderer.

06:59.640 --> 07:01.480
My men will handle his capture.

07:01.760 --> 07:03.860
Order your guards to seal off the exits!

07:04.000 --> 07:05.000
Yes, sir!

07:15.520 --> 07:17.440
HAVOC: How the hell are we
supposed to find him?

07:19.420 --> 07:21.140
We're gonna have to split up.

07:21.180 --> 07:21.880
Yes, sir.

07:31.760 --> 07:34.640
It doesn't look like anybody's
used this lab in a while.

07:34.760 --> 07:37.640
I guess not. What is this stuff?

07:38.120 --> 07:39.480
I have no idea.

07:39.780 --> 07:42.600
But whatever they did here
was painful for someone.

07:42.640 --> 07:45.400
Well now,
I am just shocked.

07:49.160 --> 07:52.040
It's bad enough that you
stood me up on our date.

07:52.620 --> 07:55.280
And now you point a gun at me?

07:56.140 --> 07:58.740
You've got some nerve,
don't you?

07:58.800 --> 07:59.920
Solaris?

08:01.200 --> 08:02.220
What's going on?

08:02.380 --> 08:03.580
Hey, Havoc...

08:03.640 --> 08:06.000
Your girl's got the tattoo.

08:06.180 --> 08:09.000
HAVOC: Yeah. First I've seen it, sir.

08:10.160 --> 08:13.160
Quit staring.
It's not very polite.

08:13.500 --> 08:16.520
MUSTANG: Well, I can see how
she tricked you so easily.

08:16.800 --> 08:18.840
You've always been
a sucker for big boobs.

08:21.720 --> 08:24.200
[CRYING] I can't help it! I love 'em!

08:26.620 --> 08:28.380
Did you tell this woman anything?

08:28.620 --> 08:31.560
No. I never said a single
thing about work, sir!

08:35.120 --> 08:38.400
Tell me. Do you know who Maes Hughes is?

08:39.600 --> 08:43.360
Oh, yes. He was quite the
intelligent man, wouldn't you agree?

08:43.540 --> 08:46.180
I only wish I'd had the opportunity to pick his brain

08:46.180 --> 08:47.000
[GUNSHOT]

08:49.000 --> 08:50.260
On your knees!

08:50.920 --> 08:52.600
I wanna know everything.

08:53.380 --> 08:55.000
Sorry to say...

08:55.900 --> 08:59.360
But it's gonna take more than you're
capable of to make me get on my—

08:59.360 --> 09:01.360
[GUNSHOTS]

09:05.260 --> 09:09.740
How merciless. Did you pick that up in Ishval, huh?

09:12.700 --> 09:14.200
You're a Homunculus.

09:14.340 --> 09:17.300
Indeed. How very astute of you, Jean.

09:17.480 --> 09:19.440
But I doubt you've seen this one.

09:24.360 --> 09:28.720
Take a good look, boys. It's a Philosopher's Stone.

09:29.760 --> 09:32.420
I was created with this stone at my core.

09:33.080 --> 09:36.180
It's not just a legend, it's my heart.

09:36.960 --> 09:38.160
You're a monster.

09:38.380 --> 09:40.080
That was uncalled for.

09:40.180 --> 09:41.860
I do have feelings.

09:42.160 --> 09:45.700
Apart from a few things, I was
made nearly identical to you.

09:46.340 --> 09:48.260
I am human.

09:50.320 --> 09:53.300
MUSTANG: I've got a funny feeling the
only reason you're telling us this...

09:53.440 --> 09:55.380
is because you don't
plan on letting us live.

09:55.660 --> 09:58.000
Yep. It's such a shame.

10:01.500 --> 10:03.000
Too slow!

10:06.820 --> 10:09.780
Oh no, did I get your
ignition glove all wet?

10:10.040 --> 10:11.300
Silly me.

10:11.300 --> 10:13.300
[BOTH YELLING]

10:17.960 --> 10:21.120
What are we gonna do? She'll shred us with her freaky fingers!

10:21.200 --> 10:22.980
No, she made a big mistake.

10:24.460 --> 10:26.480
She flooded the room with water.

10:27.160 --> 10:31.000
A simple transmutation
and we've got hydrogen gas.

10:39.060 --> 10:40.720
[BOTH GASP]

10:46.260 --> 10:47.760
Fullmetal Alchemist.

10:49.540 --> 10:51.700
Fullmetal Alchemist.

10:53.200 --> 10:54.060
HAVOC: Aw...

10:54.940 --> 10:58.380
Crap. This was a gift from
one of my ex-girlfriends.

11:00.640 --> 11:01.340
Man.

11:01.660 --> 11:04.740
Hey, Colonel.
You mind giving me a light here?

11:06.000 --> 11:07.880
Oh, right. You're all wet.

11:07.920 --> 11:10.020
Yeah, well those things will
kill you, you know that?!

11:11.420 --> 11:14.240
She's dust. I definitely cremated her.

11:14.420 --> 11:16.000
How do you know for sure, sir?

11:16.180 --> 11:17.440
The stench.

11:17.620 --> 11:20.080
I'm pretty familiar with that stink by now.

11:20.240 --> 11:22.380
You mean from that
time you spent in Ishval?

11:22.520 --> 11:24.780
For all we know, she
could still regenerate.

11:25.320 --> 11:26.500
So stay alert.

11:26.540 --> 11:27.100
Yes, sir.

11:27.740 --> 11:30.000
Ah!

11:34.280 --> 11:35.900
Havoc!

11:41.380 --> 11:43.280
MUSTANG: Havoc, hang in there.

11:43.460 --> 11:45.200
LUST: Don't kid yourself.

11:45.320 --> 11:47.320
[LAUGHS]
He's a dead man.

11:48.580 --> 11:50.360
No, he's not.

11:52.700 --> 11:53.560
Give up.

11:53.740 --> 11:56.400
There's nothing you can do that'll kill me.

11:56.600 --> 11:59.560
Then you won't mind if I borrow this!

12:11.340 --> 12:13.280
I need it to save Havoc.

12:16.380 --> 12:22.460
I don't know that much about medicinal alchemy,
but this should amplify my abilities.

12:24.940 --> 12:27.920
It seems like you should buy a girl dinner first,

12:28.000 --> 12:30.760
before you stick your hand in her chest.

12:42.600 --> 12:45.000
Uh...your Excellency!

12:46.120 --> 12:47.900
What's the current status?

12:49.100 --> 12:52.520
The criminal responsible for the
prison break has stormed the premises.

12:52.620 --> 12:54.940
But Colonel Mustang
and his men are in pursuit.

12:56.120 --> 12:58.500
Well then, I'll give him some backup.

12:58.620 --> 13:00.720
Very good. We're right behind you, sir.

13:00.820 --> 13:01.740
No.

13:03.120 --> 13:05.680
I'd prefer to handle it on my own.

13:07.680 --> 13:09.160
[LAUGHS]

13:09.160 --> 13:10.440
I told you.

13:10.940 --> 13:13.040
The Philosopher's Stone's my core.

13:18.780 --> 13:20.420
I really hate to do this.

13:20.600 --> 13:23.580
You were a prime
candidate for sacrifice and all.

13:23.760 --> 13:26.000
But you forced me to kill you.

13:26.100 --> 13:27.480
God damn you.

13:28.240 --> 13:29.480
[GLOVE TEARING]

13:30.200 --> 13:31.240
Save your breath.

13:31.300 --> 13:33.700
I want you to watch
poor Jean bleed to death.

13:33.740 --> 13:35.440
Then you can die.

13:37.580 --> 13:38.640
Jean.

13:38.700 --> 13:39.820
Hey.

13:39.980 --> 13:41.460
Answer me.

13:41.580 --> 13:42.660
Havoc!

13:42.940 --> 13:44.320
You can't die.

13:44.540 --> 13:47.280
Not yet. Not before I do.

13:48.700 --> 13:49.820
Havoc...

13:58.380 --> 13:59.500
BARRY: Sorry.

13:59.620 --> 14:01.240
But you got here too late.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.440
Look at this mess.

14:03.500 --> 14:06.340
My body is damn near entirely decayed.

14:06.740 --> 14:11.180
I guess a body just can't hold up with
someone else's soul being shoved inside of it.

14:11.320 --> 14:12.460
[AL GASPS]

14:14.540 --> 14:18.140
If a soul is incompatible
with another person's body...

14:18.500 --> 14:22.540
wouldn't it be the same for a
soul bonded to a suit of armor?

14:22.880 --> 14:24.360
If that's right...

14:24.420 --> 14:30.000
There's no guarantee I'll be able to stay in
this form long enough to get our old bodies back.

14:30.980 --> 14:31.880
Brother.

14:34.900 --> 14:38.020
I was wondering when you
were going to show up, Lusty.

14:38.240 --> 14:39.740
Number 66.

14:39.880 --> 14:42.360
Care to explain why
you're helping the Colonel?

14:42.900 --> 14:45.060
I thought it'd be fun to switch things up.

14:45.120 --> 14:50.120
Besides, I've wanted to
chop you up since I met you.

14:51.000 --> 14:53.220
You're such a handful, 66.

14:53.380 --> 14:55.780
And I'm sad to see you here, Armor Boy.

14:55.820 --> 14:57.740
You just had to tag along.

14:57.880 --> 14:59.900
Talk about a setback.

15:00.440 --> 15:05.900
It's bad enough to lose one, but now you're
forcing me to kill a second candidate.

15:06.120 --> 15:07.520
AL: Candidate?

15:07.660 --> 15:09.020
A second one?

15:09.180 --> 15:10.060
Yeah.

15:10.180 --> 15:11.900
You and Mr. Gallantry.

15:11.980 --> 15:14.400
That's enough of the
casual chit-chat, Lust!

15:14.520 --> 15:18.000
All I want to hear from you is screaming!

15:27.540 --> 15:29.840
I do hate overconfident men.

15:30.120 --> 15:32.180
Now then, where were we?

15:32.400 --> 15:35.980
I think I was about to send the
Lieutenant to join her superior.

15:36.120 --> 15:36.780
[GASPS]

15:43.820 --> 15:45.300
Wait a minute.

15:45.780 --> 15:48.940
So when you said you'd already
had to kill someone...

15:49.380 --> 15:50.700
It can't be.

15:50.880 --> 15:52.240
You didn't!

15:52.680 --> 15:53.680
[CHUCKLES]

15:54.320 --> 15:55.380
[GASPS]

15:55.760 --> 15:57.400
You bitch!

15:57.400 --> 15:59.240
[CONTINUOUS GUNFIRE]

15:59.240 --> 16:01.140
[HAWKEYE SCREAMING]

16:09.200 --> 16:10.960
[GUN CLICKING EMPTY]

16:10.960 --> 16:12.960
[GUNFIRE CONTINUES]

16:15.760 --> 16:17.160
[HAWKEYE SOBBING]

16:17.160 --> 16:19.160
[GUN CLICKS EMPTY]

16:22.280 --> 16:23.600
Are you done?

16:43.140 --> 16:45.000
Such a sad and weak creature.

16:45.240 --> 16:47.000
Another typical human.

16:51.720 --> 16:54.500
Stand up, Lieutenant. You need to get out of here.

16:54.600 --> 16:57.000
LUST: Do you want me to kill you first?

16:59.380 --> 17:00.660
[GASPS]

17:01.180 --> 17:02.260
Oh my.

17:02.420 --> 17:04.820
It appears you've opened the portal.

17:09.240 --> 17:10.660
Such a shame.

17:10.880 --> 17:13.320
You are a perfect candidate.

17:17.100 --> 17:20.520
HAWKEYE: Listen, Alphonse,
leave me and save yourself.

17:20.540 --> 17:21.300
AL: No!

17:21.340 --> 17:22.420
Run!

17:22.600 --> 17:24.600
- I won't!
- Go!

17:25.000 --> 17:26.780
I won't leave you!

17:27.900 --> 17:32.860
I'm sick of watching people die, and I
can't just sit back and take it anymore!

17:33.040 --> 17:35.200
I won't let anyone else get killed!

17:35.260 --> 17:37.520
Not when I can protect them!

17:42.920 --> 17:44.260
Well spoken.

17:44.520 --> 17:46.600
I couldn't agree more.

17:46.780 --> 17:47.440
[GASP]

17:50.200 --> 17:51.900
[LUST SCREAMING]

17:59.360 --> 18:01.820
MUSTANG: Looks like I can get you
on your knees, after all.

18:06.260 --> 18:08.340
LUST: He's using the flint for ignition...

18:08.420 --> 18:11.520
And he carved a
transmutation circle into his hand!

18:13.640 --> 18:16.000
You should have bled
to death by now!

18:16.000 --> 18:18.000
I seared the wound closed.

18:18.600 --> 18:21.300
I came close to passing out from the pain.

18:26.100 --> 18:27.860
You told me I couldn't kill you.

18:27.880 --> 18:30.720
But I'd like to try
and prove you wrong!

18:31.340 --> 18:35.000
So let's see.
How many times is it gonna take?

18:36.460 --> 18:37.860
[LUST SCREAMING]

18:37.920 --> 18:38.920
Colonel!

18:43.560 --> 18:45.160
[LUST SCREAMING] No!

18:46.740 --> 18:48.720
[LUST SCREAMING]

19:12.240 --> 19:14.240
You killed me.

19:15.380 --> 19:17.060
I hate losing.

19:17.600 --> 19:21.120
But there are worse ways to die
than at the hands of a man like you.

19:21.540 --> 19:24.600
I love how cold and
focused your eyes are.

19:24.920 --> 19:27.080
I look forward...

19:27.240 --> 19:30.960
to the day when those eyes will be wide with agony.

19:31.400 --> 19:32.580
It's coming.

19:33.180 --> 19:34.280
It's coming...

19:42.840 --> 19:43.920
Colonel!

19:46.400 --> 19:48.000
Are you alright?

19:48.060 --> 19:50.360
Forget about me.
We need to get you some help.

19:50.800 --> 19:52.220
Thanks, Alphonse.

19:52.600 --> 19:55.000
Thank you for looking
after my subordinate.

19:55.100 --> 19:57.660
Yeah, sure.
We need to call you a doctor.

19:57.740 --> 19:59.960
Oh, yeah. Hurry.

20:00.040 --> 20:01.920
Call a doctor for Havoc.

20:03.040 --> 20:03.980
Please.

20:14.940 --> 20:16.240
He's alright... He's alright...

20:21.720 --> 20:22.280
[GASP]

20:29.480 --> 20:32.700
Uh, hey.
I'm home now.

20:36.320 --> 20:38.660
Moron! Welcome back!

20:38.800 --> 20:41.900
Uh...okay! Thanks?

20:43.500 --> 20:47.800
Well...uh...

20:49.080 --> 20:51.520
[WINRY LAUGHING]

20:51.620 --> 20:54.400
[BOTH LAUGHING]

20:54.460 --> 20:56.700
[CRASH]
[BOTH YELLING]

20:56.760 --> 20:57.940
WINRY: That shouldn't happen!

20:57.980 --> 20:59.440
AL: It won't stay!

20:59.560 --> 21:01.720
AL: Ah! I can't put it back on!

21:05.360 --> 21:09.220
BARRY: Holy moly!
That was way too damn close.

21:09.460 --> 21:11.260
I hope someone can fix me.

21:11.640 --> 21:14.980
I'd rather not live
my life as sheet metal.

21:16.060 --> 21:21.000
Ahh—what the...
How the hell are you still alive?!

21:21.060 --> 21:24.240
Hey! Oh, no!
Put me down right now!

21:24.380 --> 21:27.180
I-I've got a second
chance to terrorize the city!

21:27.320 --> 21:28.840
You're gonna ruin everything!

21:28.900 --> 21:30.920
No! Don't do it! Wait!

21:30.980 --> 21:34.000
No! Stop! Please!

21:36.900 --> 21:38.200
[BARRY'S BODY THUDS]

21:41.800 --> 21:46.640
[INDISCERNIBLE]

21:46.780 --> 21:47.940
[TWINKLE]

22:08.640 --> 22:11.160
It can't be...

22:14.080 --> 22:15.920
Is it?

22:22.860 --> 22:24.320
[GASPS]

22:25.640 --> 22:27.100
Hohenheim!

22:28.860 --> 22:34.400
Let it all out, let it all out

22:34.400 --> 22:38.760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

22:39.760 --> 22:45.100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

22:45.100 --> 22:51.120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:51.580 --> 22:56.820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

22:56.820 --> 23:02.200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

23:02.720 --> 23:11.960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

23:12.160 --> 23:17.580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

23:17.660 --> 23:23.840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

23:23.840 --> 23:31.780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

23:31.780 --> 23:34.040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

23:34.040 --> 23:39.340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

23:39.340 --> 23:45.560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

23:45.560 --> 23:53.200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

23:53.440 --> 23:57.740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

24:00.400 --> 24:03.160
The truth stands between
two opposing mirrors,

24:03.220 --> 24:06.120
each casting reflections
of outrage and joy.

24:06.560 --> 24:09.340
When unexpectedly
confronted by his forsaken past,

24:09.500 --> 24:11.820
the young man is forced to resolve issues

24:11.860 --> 24:14.280
that have laid hidden within
the shadows of his anger.

24:15.000 --> 24:17.940
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:18.480 --> 24:21.740
Episode 20: Father Before the Grave.

24:22.680 --> 24:27.980
It's not necessary to shed tears.
A person can still cry without them.
